# Dependencies — keep the app dependency-free

## Context

The app ships with only `typescript` and `vitest` as devDependencies (see
`app/package.json`) and NO runtime dependencies. The exercise is about the
custom store, not about pulling in libraries.

## Rule

- Do NOT add npm packages (runtime or dev) to solve a feature. Prefer the
  standard library and the existing in-house code.
- NEVER edit `app/package.json` `dependencies`/`devDependencies` or add a
  lockfile entry without explicit user approval.
- Do NOT introduce a state-management, utility (lodash), or UI library.
- If a package genuinely seems necessary, STOP and ask the user first, naming
  the package and why the standard library is insufficient.

## How to verify

1. `git diff app/package.json` shows no dependency changes for feature work.
2. No new `import` from a bare package name (only relative `./` imports plus the
   existing `vitest` in tests).
3. `cd app && npm test` passes without installing anything new.

